  Why: 'The St Peters key-scene boards'' cliff FORM (terrain pass 9 west and east
    ledges, the south arm, the lighthouse point): regular stacked courses of near-equal
    height with a crisp dark bed line under each and a lit lip on top, thin pale
    grey-green interbeds every few courses, long slabs cut by staggered vertical
    joints, and whole blocks standing proud or sitting back so the light facets the
    wall block by block. Our shipped sandstone is warped, gated beds with plucked
    sockets; this is the same rock, aspect and batter drawn the boards'' way, through
    the kit''s own form, tiers and palette rows.'
